  "sport": "basketball",
  "title": "Through the tight cones – dribble and finish",
  "description": "Set five or six cones in a row towards the basket with only about half a metre between them. Every player has a ball and lines up behind the first cone. The player works along the row with the cones between their feet and does a dribble combination between each cone – the ball should bounce in the gap between two cones without touching them. After the last cone the player takes one long dribble straight at the basket and finishes with a lay-up or a shot, grabs the rebound and dribbles back down the side to the line.\n\nChange the combination every round: single, double and triple crossover, between the legs, side to side. Let players mix up their finishes.\n\nHarder: more cones (all the way to half-court) or tighter gaps. Easier: wider gaps and the last cone closer to the basket. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Hips low and chest up all the way through the cones."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Short, quick steps – chop your feet and keep the ball close."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Push the speed until you sometimes lose it; that is where you improve."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Last dribble: straight at the basket, no detours."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
